WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.270 --> 00:00:02.070
- All right, let's finish
things up with a story

00:00:02.070 --> 00:00:03.360
I hope will warm your heart.

00:00:03.360 --> 00:00:04.539
This is What I'm Liking.

00:00:04.539 --> 00:00:07.770
(upbeat music)

00:00:07.770 --> 00:00:10.320
So not long ago, a
Virginia woman named Anna

00:00:10.320 --> 00:00:13.560
was rearranging some furniture
and discovered a small door

00:00:13.560 --> 00:00:15.900
in her closet she never knew existed.

00:00:15.900 --> 00:00:18.030
When she opened it up,
she discovered boxes

00:00:18.030 --> 00:00:20.250
of handwritten letters from the fifties.

00:00:20.250 --> 00:00:25.250
Many of them romantic variety
between Betty Sue and Vance.

00:00:25.530 --> 00:00:27.930
She knew that she had to
get these love letters back

00:00:27.930 --> 00:00:29.190
to the original owners.

00:00:29.190 --> 00:00:32.670
So she did what people do in
2022 and took to social media.

00:00:32.670 --> 00:00:35.340
And internet sleuths came through.

00:00:35.340 --> 00:00:38.910
Turns out Betty Sue and Vance
eventually did get married

00:00:38.910 --> 00:00:42.180
and Anna was able to connect
with their grandsons.

00:00:42.180 --> 00:00:44.310
We have all of them dialed in right now.

00:00:44.310 --> 00:00:47.370
Anna and Bodie are each
watching in Richmond, Virginia

00:00:47.370 --> 00:00:48.570
on NBC 12.

00:00:48.570 --> 00:00:51.840
And Dalton's in Portland
watching on Fox 12 Oregon.

00:00:51.840 --> 00:00:52.690
What's up, y'all?

00:00:54.264 --> 00:00:56.166
- Hi.
- Hi Kelly.

00:00:56.166 --> 00:00:57.060
- Hi.

00:00:57.060 --> 00:00:58.770
So Anna, I'm gonna start with you.

00:00:58.770 --> 00:01:01.950
What did you think when you
first discovered the letters?

00:01:01.950 --> 00:01:05.010
- This story is like "Goonies"
meets "The Notebook."

00:01:05.010 --> 00:01:07.560
I'm a 1980's baby, so I'm
obsessed with the movie "Goonies."

00:01:07.560 --> 00:01:08.770
- Yes.

00:01:08.770 --> 00:01:09.630
- And I'm thinking I'm gonna
go into this crawlspace,

00:01:09.630 --> 00:01:12.720
slash attic, and I'm going to find a map

00:01:12.720 --> 00:01:14.760
that's gonna lead me to
Willy Wonka's treasure,

00:01:14.760 --> 00:01:17.490
or to gold coins that
were gonna make me rich.

00:01:17.490 --> 00:01:21.030
But I ended up just finding
creepy looking dolls,

00:01:21.030 --> 00:01:23.490
and Christmas ornaments, and bills,

00:01:23.490 --> 00:01:24.480
and things of that nature.

00:01:24.480 --> 00:01:27.240
But I did go in the corner
and I found these two boxes

00:01:27.240 --> 00:01:29.940
of hundreds and hundreds of letters.

00:01:29.940 --> 00:01:31.530
I thought to myself, at that point,

00:01:31.530 --> 00:01:34.320
if these letters were
out there in my family,

00:01:34.320 --> 00:01:36.690
I would absolutely want
them in our possession.

00:01:36.690 --> 00:01:38.490
So that's when I went to social media

00:01:38.490 --> 00:01:40.200
to look for someone in the family.

00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:42.840
At first, I was really
concerned about privacy.

00:01:42.840 --> 00:01:45.180
But then I kicked that
angel off my shoulder

00:01:45.180 --> 00:01:47.485
and invited my sisters
over and we drank some wine

00:01:47.485 --> 00:01:49.200
and read the letters.

00:01:49.200 --> 00:01:50.760
And it turns out it was a love story

00:01:50.760 --> 00:01:53.220
between Bodie and Dalton's grandparents.

00:01:53.220 --> 00:01:55.380
And obviously awesome,
really dynamic people.

00:01:55.380 --> 00:01:56.460
She was a basketball player.

00:01:56.460 --> 00:01:59.070
He was a baseball player,
high school sweethearts.

00:01:59.070 --> 00:02:00.120
They fell in love.

00:02:00.120 --> 00:02:03.420
At least 60% of the letters
were from those two.

00:02:03.420 --> 00:02:05.460
There were more, I mean, men will be men,

00:02:05.460 --> 00:02:07.590
and in 1950 it was no
different than it is now.

00:02:07.590 --> 00:02:08.880
They were chasing after Betty Sue

00:02:08.880 --> 00:02:10.667
pretty hard in those letters.

00:02:10.667 --> 00:02:11.500
(Kelly laughing)

00:02:11.500 --> 00:02:14.550
Vance won in the end, obviously.

00:02:14.550 --> 00:02:16.380
So I was thrilled to get
the letters to these guys

00:02:16.380 --> 00:02:18.810
so they can read about their
grandparents' courtship.

00:02:18.810 --> 00:02:19.680
- I love that.

00:02:19.680 --> 00:02:21.180
So Dalton and Bodie,

00:02:21.180 --> 00:02:24.120
what did you think when you
learned about these letters?

00:02:24.120 --> 00:02:26.987
- So my first thought was how did we live

00:02:26.987 --> 00:02:29.250
in this house for 18 years

00:02:29.250 --> 00:02:32.640
and have no idea that these
letters were in the house?

00:02:32.640 --> 00:02:34.440
And then immediately after that,

00:02:34.440 --> 00:02:36.930
I was thinking about how Dalton

00:02:36.930 --> 00:02:41.580
and I were gonna get a very
personable understanding

00:02:41.580 --> 00:02:44.250
of our grandparents when they were young.

00:02:44.250 --> 00:02:47.010
And that was super
exciting for both of us.

00:02:47.010 --> 00:02:50.144
I was, actually the
latest letter that I read,

00:02:50.144 --> 00:02:54.600
talked about how my grandfather
had been given an offer

00:02:54.600 --> 00:02:57.270
to play professional
baseball in a summer league

00:02:57.270 --> 00:02:58.860
down in Florida.

00:02:58.860 --> 00:03:01.920
And they wanted him to leave the next day.

00:03:01.920 --> 00:03:04.020
So he started packing his bags

00:03:04.020 --> 00:03:05.940
and getting his affairs in order.

00:03:05.940 --> 00:03:10.200
And in the midst of all that,
he realized there was no way

00:03:10.200 --> 00:03:13.170
that he was gonna spend three plus months

00:03:13.170 --> 00:03:16.590
without my grandmother,
being four states away.

00:03:16.590 --> 00:03:19.200
So we decided to say no to the offer

00:03:19.200 --> 00:03:22.020
so that he could be closer to my grandma.

00:03:22.020 --> 00:03:24.540
And this letter, actually,
that I just showed you

00:03:24.540 --> 00:03:27.007
in the end, the letter closed with,

00:03:27.007 --> 00:03:30.750
"If you are a dream, I
hope to never be awoken,"

00:03:30.750 --> 00:03:32.460
which is very poetic.

00:03:32.460 --> 00:03:33.570
- I love that.

00:03:33.570 --> 00:03:36.960
And Betty Sue, boy, she
was like, all right,

00:03:36.960 --> 00:03:37.950
go ahead, leave.

00:03:37.950 --> 00:03:39.660
And he was like, nevermind.

00:03:39.660 --> 00:03:41.250
He was like, so Dalton,

00:03:41.250 --> 00:03:43.380
what did you think about the letters?

00:03:43.380 --> 00:03:45.990
- I mean, I thought it was super romantic.

00:03:45.990 --> 00:03:48.420
Bodie and I were both very lucky

00:03:48.420 --> 00:03:50.160
'cause our grandparents were actually

00:03:50.160 --> 00:03:52.770
just a few houses down
when we were growing up.

00:03:52.770 --> 00:03:54.660
So we had a super close relationship.

00:03:54.660 --> 00:03:59.660
And we got to see them in love
at the end of their lives.

00:03:59.820 --> 00:04:03.450
But then, you know, recently
our father passed away

00:04:03.450 --> 00:04:05.580
and he was kind of our last connection

00:04:05.580 --> 00:04:07.350
to that side of the family.

00:04:07.350 --> 00:04:08.940
And so we didn't really have much

00:04:08.940 --> 00:04:10.500
until these letters popped up.

00:04:10.500 --> 00:04:13.470
And they've kind of become
like the last heirloom.

00:04:13.470 --> 00:04:18.030
And I'm just really excited
to explore their love

00:04:18.030 --> 00:04:21.510
and get to know our grandparents
when they were my age

00:04:21.510 --> 00:04:22.950
or even a little younger.

00:04:22.950 --> 00:04:26.706
- Yeah, I love that. That's so special.

00:04:26.706 --> 00:04:27.539
Thank you so much, Anna.

00:04:27.539 --> 00:04:28.590
That's so cool.

00:04:28.590 --> 00:04:29.700
You didn't find buried treasure,

00:04:29.700 --> 00:04:31.550
but you found buried treasure for them.

00:04:31.550 --> 00:04:33.901
- No, that's right, that's right.

00:04:33.901 --> 00:04:34.750
- [Bodie] Very true.

00:04:34.750 --> 00:04:35.583
- So thank you, Anna.

00:04:35.583 --> 00:04:36.416
I would've read them too.

00:04:36.416 --> 00:04:37.590
I wouldn't have even needed wine.

00:04:37.590 --> 00:04:40.050
I'd have been like, I
gotta know what this is.

00:04:40.050 --> 00:04:42.570
Dalton and Bodie, thank you
so much is well for sharing.

00:04:42.570 --> 00:04:45.570
I'm liking y'alls post
right now, all right?

00:04:45.570 --> 00:04:46.403
- [Bodie] Thank you.

00:04:46.403 --> 00:04:47.236
- Yeah, absolutely.

00:04:47.236 --> 00:04:48.960
And that's not all our season long partner

00:04:48.960 --> 00:04:51.060
Pilot Pen makers of G2, the go-to pen

00:04:51.060 --> 00:04:52.650
of "The Kelly Clarkson Show,"

00:04:52.650 --> 00:04:54.600
thinks this story is as sweet as we do.

00:04:54.600 --> 00:04:56.310
So they're gonna be writing you a check

00:04:56.310 --> 00:04:57.426
for $1000 for you all to split.

00:04:57.426 --> 00:04:58.911
So there you go.

00:04:58.911 --> 00:05:01.494
(all praising)

00:05:02.453 --> 00:05:04.720
All right, thank y'all so much.

